rem Circular Logic
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=209
rem Count N-input truth tables t with
rem t(x) and t(g(x)) never both true,
rem where g shifts in a xor (b and c)

use bits
use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 6

rem g permutes the 2^N inputs, so it
rem splits into cycles. A table on
rem a cycle of length k has no two
rem neighbours set in Lucas(k) ways, and
rem the cycles are independent. Each
rem input takes the least label on its
rem cycle by repeated neighbour mins.
S = 1 N shl
X = 0 till S array
A = X (N - 1) bit
B = X (N - 2) bit
C = X (N - 3) bit
Bc = B and C
Nw = A not equal Bc
Low = X mod (S // 2)
G = Low * 2 + (Nw choose 1 0)
Lab = X
for I in 1 to S
  Lab = Lab (Lab G) min
end
Own = Lab equal X
Col = X reshape S 1
Size = (Lab equal Col) count axis 1
Lens = Size filter Own array
Fs = fibonacci take (S + 2) array
Fib = concat (array 0 1) Fs
Luc = (Fib take S) + (Fib drop 2 take S)
Answer = (Luc (Lens - 1)) reduce *
Answer print
